      "id": 50583761,
      "title": "Ask HN: I have been unemployed for 2y. 15 years of experience, US. What to do?",
      "url": "",
      "domain": "",
      "author": "LetThingsBeDiff",
      "score": 728,
      "comments": 825,
      "time": 1795216712,
      "text": "I&#x27;m Senior software engineer in the US (DMV area), with 15y of experience. Worked for Fortune 50+ company and bunch of mid-size companies. Been unemployed for 2y and can&#x27;t find a job, within those 2 years, I pretty much spent my savings that I&#x27;ve saved through years, maybe have 4-5 months left to support my household. Currently, I tutor math and probably about to start working as manager in pizzaria.<p>In Jan 2025, I quit from a mid-size insurance tech company(1000+) after working there for almost 4y, because I was tipped off the they were about to start layoffs and they did. Well, since then I have zero luck finding any job in SWE.<p>At this point, I have massive gap in my resume that I can&#x27;t explain to recruiters, I can still code (C#&#x2F;.NET&#x2F;AWS) and learned the AI, but who cares if date of my last employment is Jan2025. What should I do ?<p>If you have an alternative path (something completely different from SWE or SWE adjacent) that pays &quot;well&quot;, I would like to hear."
    },
